These files are generated Wireshark dissectors. They are published so that you
can read your own captures with them.


What you may do

You may use, copy and modify these files, and you may compile them into a
Wireshark that you build and run yourself, for your own use, without charge
and without asking.


What is reserved

Only the Open Markets Initiative and William Tegel may place this code
into the Wireshark build. That means:

  - submitting it to the Wireshark project, at wireshark/wireshark or elsewhere
  - including it in a Wireshark distribution, package, image or installer
  - distributing any Wireshark binary built with it

Those rights are reserved by the copyright holders and are not granted here.
Publishing this code is not an offer of it to the Wireshark project.


Wireshark's own license

Wireshark is licensed GPL-2.0-or-later. A dissector compiled into Wireshark
forms a combined work with it, and Wireshark's license governs what you may
do when you distribute that combined work. Nothing here restricts a build you
make for yourself and do not distribute, which is what these files are for.
The reservation above is on placing this code into builds given to others; it
does not purport to add conditions to Wireshark itself.


